201 Created
Successful post request committed. Entity saved to disk.
Update views or navigate to confirmation immediately.
400 Bad Request
Parser or validation engine failed to validate payload.
Parse response errors to individual form field feedback.
401 Unauthorized
New secure session creation: auth variables required.
Clear credentials, trigger token refreshes, or force logout.
429 Too Many Requests
Throttling limits hit based on server-side IP tracking.
Delay requests by reading backoff seconds in headers.

Best Practices (أفضل الممارسات التقنية)
	1	Never use any: Ensure all system fetch methods return compiled types inferred from validations rather than fallback any types.
	2	Explicitly Set Headers on API Calls: Always double check request types. If your payload is JSON, always declare 'Content-Type': 'application/json' to prevent body parse errors on server endpoints.
	3	Use Safe JSON Decoders: Decoders like standard JSON.parse inside raw environments can crash application processes if the payload is corrupted. Protect parses with defensive try/catch boundaries.

